    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623">

                <pb facs="0760" n="664" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg664"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-11-03"><hi rendition="#italic">November 3,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>If there is any doubt of the American attitude as to partition of Samoa, you may
                    say to Lord Salisbury that we are favorable to it, provided <pb facs="0761"
                        n="665" xml:id="pg665"/> that satisfactory terms can be made, and that we
                    shall be content with that portion of the islands east of the one hundred and
                    seventy-first meridian.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
